Consider the differential equation on the region $x>0$, $y>0$:

$$
y^3\,\mathrm{d}x+(xy^2+y)\,\mathrm{d}y=0.
$$

Test whether $I(x,y)=\dfrac{e^{xy}}{y}$ is an integrating factor. Record the coefficients after multiplication and the two derivatives needed to justify your conclusion.

In $I\bigl[y^3\,\mathrm{d}x+(xy^2+y)\,\mathrm{d}y\bigr]=M\,\mathrm{d}x+N\,\mathrm{d}y$,

$M=$ {{field-1}}

$N=$ {{field-2}}

$M_y=$ {{field-3}}

$N_x=$ {{field-4}}

The proposed function {{field-5}} an integrating factor.

